{"id":"ac1f08ea179b507d63db479978f72c9e867d8e72","axis":"silent","repo":"systemd/systemd","sha":"ac1f08ea179b507d63db479978f72c9e867d8e72","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"man/sysupdate.components.xml","lines":["@@ -116,6 +116,25 @@","         <xi:include href=\"version-info.xml\" xpointer=\"v262\"/></listitem>","       </varlistentry>"," ","+      <varlistentry>","+        <term><varname>SuccessAction=</varname></term>","+","+        <listitem><para>Controls what to do after an update of this component has been installed","+        successfully, when multiple components are updated in one go (i.e. when","+        <command>systemd-sysupdate update</command> is invoked with <option>--component-all</option>). Takes","+        one of <literal>continue</literal> or <literal>restart</literal>. If <literal>continue</literal>,","+        the update logic proceeds with the next component. If <literal>restart</literal>, the remaining","+        components are skipped and the current update iteration is finished early, so that the next","+        iteration starts from the beginning, re-reading all definition files. This is useful for components","+        that make new transfer files (or components) available, which should be processed before any other","+        components are updated. Note that the next iteration is only started if the","+        <option>--loop=</option> switch permits it, see","+        <citerefentry><refentrytitle>systemd-sysupdate</refentrytitle><manvolnum>8</manvolnum></citerefentry>","+        for details. Defaults to <literal>continue</literal>.</para>","+","+        <xi:include href=\"version-info.xml\" xpointer=\"v263\"/></listitem>","+      </varlistentry>","+","       <varlistentry>","         <term><varname>Suggest=</varname></term>"," "],"additions":19,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/sysupdate/sysupdate-config.c","lines":["@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@"," "," #include \"alloc-util.h\""," #include \"condition.h\"","+#include \"conf-parser.h\""," #incl